                        "form": "die Mehrdeutigkeiten"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "24e862ee-dff0-350e-818e-3b449dfa1c66",
                        "entry_id": "c35255e8-0b23-3aae-aeee-4769772ba648",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Möglichkeit unterschiedlicher Interpretation eines Gegebenen, eines Sachverhalts, einer Lehre oder von sprachlichen Ausdrücken"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "general"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "29f11c8b-2c9d-4c4f-96fd-1b45e268d068",
                                "sense_id": "24e862ee-dff0-350e-818e-3b449dfa1c66",
                                "text": "Wenn jemand einen Ring trägt, kann für den Außenstehenden Mehrdeutigkeit vorliegen: Ist er ein reiner Schmuck oder zeigt er eine Freundschaft, Verlobung oder Ehe an?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "90ed32ab-0207-47d7-98e2-9f488940dbc2",
                                "sense_id": "24e862ee-dff0-350e-818e-3b449dfa1c66",
                                "text": "„Diese unberechenbare Mehrdeutigkeit hat uns schon immer beunruhigt.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7411f707-255a-3a1e-a1c3-00a0ae7aa7fd",
                        "entry_id": "c35255e8-0b23-3aae-aeee-4769772ba648",
                        "glosses": [
                            "unterschiedliche Interpretationsmöglichkeit speziell von Wörtern oder Sätzen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6dd52c87-c161-4c1b-8077-2c351158d81b",
                                "sense_id": "7411f707-255a-3a1e-a1c3-00a0ae7aa7fd",
                                "text": "Mehrdeutigkeit gibt es bei Wörtern und Sätzen; sie wird meist durch den Kontext aufgelöst."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25157187-111c-4d62-81f4-96fb3a63a0ad",
                                "sense_id": "7411f707-255a-3a1e-a1c3-00a0ae7aa7fd",
                                "text": "Mehrdeutigkeit liegt z.B. bei dem Wort \"Flügel\" vor, solange es isoliert genannt ist: Organ eines Vogels, Teil einer Mannschaft oder Tasteninstrument?"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "65a93719-9e06-4b3d-b7ea-9a934abe1832",
                        "source_entry_id": "c35255e8-0b23-3aae-aeee-4769772ba648",
                        "source_sense_id": "24e862ee-dff0-350e-818e-3b449dfa1c66",
                        "target_lang_word": "ambiguity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ambiguity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aefef315-5542-39eb-887c-cd977f8811a3",
                                        "entry_id": "fe856398-c0d8-3ac5-a71a-62063c91bdf1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being ambiguous; the state of leaving room for more than one interpretation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dba432b-8b82-4b83-bf66-4f9bf56cfaa0",
                                                "sense_id": "aefef315-5542-39eb-887c-cd977f8811a3",
                                                "text": "His speech was made with such great ambiguity that neither supporter nor opponent could be certain of his true position."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5592aea-f392-41da-80f7-68466a37aed2",
                                                "sense_id": "aefef315-5542-39eb-887c-cd977f8811a3",
                                                "text": "Whan this ſayd monument diſcouered was / Suche a ſuauite and fragrant odoure / Aſcended from the corps by ſingular grace / Paſſyng all worldly ſwetnes and ſauour / That all there present that day and hour / Suppoſed they had ben / in the felicite / Of erthely paradiſe / without ambiguite."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "307b5f88-5d72-3050-b802-d44c87e5efdd",
                                        "entry_id": "fe856398-c0d8-3ac5-a71a-62063c91bdf1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An instance of this state: words or statements that are open to more than one interpretation, explanation or meaning, especially if that meaning cannot be determined from the context."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44f83797-11ca-4ac8-a0a0-d4b938a66e69",
                                                "sense_id": "307b5f88-5d72-3050-b802-d44c87e5efdd",
                                                "text": "If two persons bore the same name, and confusion was likely to be caused, ambiguity was avoided by adding the name of the father[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c305ed61-1f5b-4e4c-9544-528f661375b9",
                                                "sense_id": "307b5f88-5d72-3050-b802-d44c87e5efdd",
                                                "text": "For people who would rather face a plague of locusts than permit an avoidable ambiguity, this is like having their underwear twisted. You may think we should say to such people, “Get a life.” By all means tell them that. I’m neither making these rules up nor trying to enforce them; my job in this book is to point out to you what seems to be the current state of the language and its speakers.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "de6da6ac-7ce9-4b93-9267-12a64f0166bd",
                        "source_entry_id": "c35255e8-0b23-3aae-aeee-4769772ba648",
                        "source_sense_id": "24e862ee-dff0-350e-818e-3b449dfa1c66",
                        "target_lang_word": "ambiguïté",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ambiguïté",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5561ce27-ae55-385e-87b2-f982a361bd85",
                                        "entry_id": "05db3df9-1d11-31de-9675-9762587a8387",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "État de ce qui est ambigu, de ce qui peut être compris dans deux sens différents ou plus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "165ee1a3-3755-42db-9ad3-f6db9dc64746",
                                                "sense_id": "5561ce27-ae55-385e-87b2-f982a361bd85",
                                                "text": "En l'état actuel des grammaires locales de levée d’ambiguïté, de très nombreuses configurations syntaxiques sont opaques et elles devraient le rester très longtemps, d'ici à ce que l'on puisse à coup sûr les soumettre à des automatismes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61bc2bf2-374f-4681-bc4c-de44232bdaab",
                                                "sense_id": "5561ce27-ae55-385e-87b2-f982a361bd85",
                                                "text": "La conséquence de ce complexe d’ambivalences est une série d’ambiguïtés aux niveaux différents du statut du texte littéraire, du traitement didactique de ce texte, et des fonctions de l'enseignant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e832b97-8e1c-47ca-8145-4ef33b0ae4fc",
                                                "sense_id": "5561ce27-ae55-385e-87b2-f982a361bd85",
                                                "text": "Faire hésiter le spectateur entre sa réalité et celle que le spectacle lui propose, cʼest ce que J. Morel a appelé à propos du théâtre de Rotrou, la dramaturgie de lʼambiguïté."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f36759b3-73e3-456d-87af-48f49dd23f04",
                                                "sense_id": "5561ce27-ae55-385e-87b2-f982a361bd85",
                                                "text": "Le philosophe doit éviter les ambiguïtés ou les plurivocités, et décider du langage qu'il entend au juste parler. Dans le cas contraire, les portes sont grandes ouvertes aux malentendus."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "13e18da7-3508-4061-9774-cacc9624f3d8",
                        "source_entry_id": "c35255e8-0b23-3aae-aeee-4769772ba648",
                        "source_sense_id": "7411f707-255a-3a1e-a1c3-00a0ae7aa7fd",
                        "source_sense_description": "Linguistik: unterschiedliche Interpretationsmöglichkeit speziell von Wörtern oder Sätzen",
                        "target_lang_word": "ambiguity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ambiguity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aefef315-5542-39eb-887c-cd977f8811a3",
                                        "entry_id": "fe856398-c0d8-3ac5-a71a-62063c91bdf1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being ambiguous; the state of leaving room for more than one interpretation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dba432b-8b82-4b83-bf66-4f9bf56cfaa0",
                                                "sense_id": "aefef315-5542-39eb-887c-cd977f8811a3",
                                                "text": "His speech was made with such great ambiguity that neither supporter nor opponent could be certain of his true position."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5592aea-f392-41da-80f7-68466a37aed2",
                                                "sense_id": "aefef315-5542-39eb-887c-cd977f8811a3",
                                                "text": "Whan this ſayd monument diſcouered was / Suche a ſuauite and fragrant odoure / Aſcended from the corps by ſingular grace / Paſſyng all worldly ſwetnes and ſauour / That all there present that day and hour / Suppoſed they had ben / in the felicite / Of erthely paradiſe / without ambiguite."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "307b5f88-5d72-3050-b802-d44c87e5efdd",
                                        "entry_id": "fe856398-c0d8-3ac5-a71a-62063c91bdf1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An instance of this state: words or statements that are open to more than one interpretation, explanation or meaning, especially if that meaning cannot be determined from the context."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44f83797-11ca-4ac8-a0a0-d4b938a66e69",
                                                "sense_id": "307b5f88-5d72-3050-b802-d44c87e5efdd",
                                                "text": "If two persons bore the same name, and confusion was likely to be caused, ambiguity was avoided by adding the name of the father[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c305ed61-1f5b-4e4c-9544-528f661375b9",
                                                "sense_id": "307b5f88-5d72-3050-b802-d44c87e5efdd",
                                                "text": "For people who would rather face a plague of locusts than permit an avoidable ambiguity, this is like having their underwear twisted. You may think we should say to such people, “Get a life.” By all means tell them that. I’m neither making these rules up nor trying to enforce them; my job in this book is to point out to you what seems to be the current state of the language and its speakers.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ff921d32-828c-46b9-b666-52895793068a",
                        "source_entry_id": "c35255e8-0b23-3aae-aeee-4769772ba648",
                        "source_sense_id": "7411f707-255a-3a1e-a1c3-00a0ae7aa7fd",
                        "source_sense_description": "Linguistik: unterschiedliche Interpretationsmöglichkeit speziell von Wörtern oder Sätzen",
                        "target_lang_word": "ambiguïté",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ambiguïté",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5561ce27-ae55-385e-87b2-f982a361bd85",
                                        "entry_id": "05db3df9-1d11-31de-9675-9762587a8387",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "État de ce qui est ambigu, de ce qui peut être compris dans deux sens différents ou plus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "165ee1a3-3755-42db-9ad3-f6db9dc64746",
                                                "sense_id": "5561ce27-ae55-385e-87b2-f982a361bd85",
                                                "text": "En l'état actuel des grammaires locales de levée d’ambiguïté, de très nombreuses configurations syntaxiques sont opaques et elles devraient le rester très longtemps, d'ici à ce que l'on puisse à coup sûr les soumettre à des automatismes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61bc2bf2-374f-4681-bc4c-de44232bdaab",
                                                "sense_id": "5561ce27-ae55-385e-87b2-f982a361bd85",
                                                "text": "La conséquence de ce complexe d’ambivalences est une série d’ambiguïtés aux niveaux différents du statut du texte littéraire, du traitement didactique de ce texte, et des fonctions de l'enseignant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e832b97-8e1c-47ca-8145-4ef33b0ae4fc",
                                                "sense_id": "5561ce27-ae55-385e-87b2-f982a361bd85",
                                                "text": "Faire hésiter le spectateur entre sa réalité et celle que le spectacle lui propose, cʼest ce que J. Morel a appelé à propos du théâtre de Rotrou, la dramaturgie de lʼambiguïté."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f36759b3-73e3-456d-87af-48f49dd23f04",
                                                "sense_id": "5561ce27-ae55-385e-87b2-f982a361bd85",
                                                "text": "Le philosophe doit éviter les ambiguïtés ou les plurivocités, et décider du langage qu'il entend au juste parler. Dans le cas contraire, les portes sont grandes ouvertes aux malentendus."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
